  "weekLabel": "Week of Oct 12–16, 2026",
  "headline": "Two bigger biotechs test a soft market",
  "summary": "Two biotech IPOs are on deck this week: AI drug designer Iambic Therapeutics (~$150M, expected Thu) and RNAi developer City Therapeutics (~$175M, Fri per IPOScoop). Last week's biotechs disappointed: TRex Bio priced at the low end and finished flat, and Retension ended down 12%. Renaissance's IPO Index fell 0.5% vs the S&P 500's +1.2% and is trading below its 50-day average. Nscale's reported mid-October date hasn't materialized (still no terms on file), and Wall Street is holding money back for Anthropic, whose public S-1 Renaissance expects as soon as Oct 23 (unconfirmed). Filings picked up: seven sizable companies filed, led by DayOne Data Centers (~$3B est.) and Nigerian fintech OPay (~$500M est.).",
  "highlights": [
    {
      "text": "Iambic (IAM) and City Therapeutics (CTY) aim to raise ~$325M combined this week",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Anthropic's public S-1 could land as soon as Oct 23; investor day reportedly Oct 14",
      "unconfirmed": true,
      "note": "Reported, not confirmed"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nscale still has no price range on file and isn't on this week's calendars",
      "unconfirmed": true,
      "note": "Timing never confirmed"
    },
    {
      "text": "OPay (~$500M est.) and vVardis (~$200M est.) filed publicly for NYSE IPOs",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Oura remains postponed with no new date; Amaero revived at ~62% smaller",
      "unconfirmed": false
    }
  ],
